The 42 puzzles were newly generated for this test with the puzzle generators released by
Taylor Webb, Keith Holyoak and Hongjing Lu for "Emergent analogical reasoning in large language models"
(Nature Human Behaviour, 2023): https://github.com/taylorwwebb/emergent_analogies_LLM (Apache License 2.0).
The student percentages that set each rung come from that paper's released human data.

The chess puzzle is from the Lichess puzzle database (CC0): https://lichess.org/training/13iFr

ELIZA ran as Anthony Hay's eliza.cpp (CC0) with the DOCTOR script from Weizenbaum's 1966 paper.
Stockfish 19 (GPL-3.0), llama.cpp (MIT), GPT-2 XL (MIT), TinyLlama (Apache-2.0) and Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
(Apache-2.0) were used to produce the answers; none of them is included here.
